.Dd February 1, 2026
.Dt PANIC 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm panic
.Nd bring down the system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/panic.h
.Ft void
.Fn panic "const char *fmt, ..."
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn panic
function terminates the running system.
The message
.Fa fmt
is a
.Xr printf 9
style format string.
The message is printed to the console and the system halts or reboots, depending on configuration and context.
.Pp
This function never returns.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kprint 9 ,
.Xr printf 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn panic
function first appeared in Substrate.
